          ],
          "content": "Revise, Reflect, Refine"
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.797,
            0.107,
            0.847,
            0.156
          ],
          "content": ""
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.236,
            0.17,
            0.888,
            0.205
          ],
          "content": "1. Meristematic tissues divide repeatedly. What property of their cells allows them to do this?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.268,
            0.207,
            0.633,
            0.225
          ],
          "content": "(i) They have thick walls for protection."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.261,
            0.225,
            0.736,
            0.242
          ],
          "content": "(ii) They contain large vacuoles that store nutrients."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.258,
            0.242,
            0.888,
            0.275
          ],
          "content": "(iii) They have thin walls, dense cytoplasm and large prominent nucleus."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.258,
            0.275,
            0.675,
            0.294
          ],
          "content": "(iv) They are functionally differentiated cells."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.235,
            0.295,
            0.888,
            0.402
          ],
          "content": "2. If a plant is unable to transport food from leaves to roots which tissue is malfunctioning? (i) Xylem (ii) Phloem (iii) Epidermis (iv) Sclerenchyma"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.04,
            0.423,
            0.222,
            0.589
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.104,
                0.595,
                0.17,
                0.611
              ],
              "content": "Fig. 3.21"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_16_image_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.236,
            0.404,
            0.888,
            0.51
          ],
          "content": "3. Why are the epithelial tissues that line an animal’s internal organs usually only one or a few cells thick? (i) To store food efficiently. (ii) To provide maximum strength. (iii) To allow quick exchange of materials across them. (iv) To reduce friction."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.236,
            0.513,
            0.889,
            0.611
          ],
          "content": "4. You can perform these two jumps (Fig. 3.21): Straight-leg jump — keep knees and ankles stiff. Normal jump — bend knees and ankles naturally. How did your ankle, knee and hip positions differ between the two jumps?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.235,
            0.611,
            0.887,
            0.685
          ],
          "content": "5. Which type of joint is involved when you bend your knees and ankles? (i) Ball and socket (ii) Hinge (iii) Pivot"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.235,
            0.687,
            0.887,
            0.721
          ],
          "content": "6. In each of the following cases (A, B, C and D), choose the correct option as given below:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.268,
            0.72,
            0.884,
            0.739
          ],
          "content": "(i) Both (A) and (R) are true, and (R) is the correct explanation of (A)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.261,
            0.739,
            0.888,
            0.771
          ],
          "content": "Both (A) and (R) are true, but (R) is not the correct explanation of (A)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.258,
            0.771,
            0.535,
            0.789
          ],
          "content": "(iii) (A) is true, but (R) is false."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.259,
            0.789,
            0.535,
            0.806
          ],
          "content": "(iv) (A) is false, but (R) is true."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.264,
            0.809,
            0.888,
            0.863
          ],
          "content": "A. Assertion: Epithelium is well-suited for gas exchange in the lungs. Reason: It consists of multiple layers of tall cells that slow down diffusion."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.265,
            0.864,
            0.889,
            0.936
          ],
          "content": "B. Assertion: Cardiac muscle can contract continuously without fatigue. Reason: Cardiac muscle cells have a high number of mitochondria and an abundant blood supply."
        },
        {
